@* U-28: friendly landing for authenticated-but-unprovisioned users. A page's [Authorize(Policy)]
   is enforced at the Blazor endpoint, so a no-role user gets a raw 403 before any component renders
   (the <NotAuthorized> in Routes.razor never runs for endpoint-level denials). A 403 status-code page
   redirects here. This route only requires an authenticated user (the fallback policy), which a
   no-role user satisfies, so it always renders. *@
@page "/access-denied"
@attribute [Authorize]
@using IncidentManager.Web.Components.Shared

<PageTitle>No access — CaseBook</PageTitle>

<AccessDenied />
